\code{vegan::decostand(method = "hellinger")}. With \code{"chord"}, the function
uses \code{vegan::decostand(method = "normalize", MARGIN = 1)}. Unconstrained
PCA is then performed using \code{vegan::rda()}; site and species scores
are extracted with \code{scaling = 2}.

Site groups can be displayed as convex hulls (\code{area = "hull"}),
95-percent normal-data ellipses (\code{"ellipse"}), or points alone
(\code{"none"}). Hulls require at least three non-collinear observations
